course: dictionary
lesson: 4546
title: Hearty words
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Heartiness is a noun, a thing you can have. It names the warm, cheerful energy someone shows, their strength and good health, or how large and filling a meal is. The word comes from heart, which helps: it is often about feeling warm inside.
explain: «The heartiness of a greeting» is about how someone says hello: loud, friendly and full of energy. Read the words around it. Greeting tells you people are meeting, so heartiness must mean warm, cheerful friendliness. Try your meaning in the sentence: "the warm friendliness of a greeting" still makes sense.
explain: Sometimes there can be a bit too much of it. In the stories, Toad «greets friends with great heartiness», which means he greets them with a lot of warm energy. A hearty welcome can be lovely, but a huge, loud one can feel like too much. The clues around the word help you feel which it is.
fact: Heartiness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say some heartiness, not two heartinesses.
fact: Meaning 1: warmth, friendliness and cheerful energy.
fact: Meaning 2: strength and good health.
fact: Meaning 3: of food, large, filling and satisfying.
fact: In the stories, Toad «greets friends with great heartiness».
exercise: «The heartiness of a greeting» shows how someone says hello. What does heartiness mean here? | Cold silence | Dirty hands | *Warm, cheerful friendliness | Being very tired
exercise: Which meaning of heartiness fits a bowl of soup that fills you right up? | Very quiet | *Large, filling and satisfying | Lost and alone | Cheerful and friendly
exercise: Grandad still walks miles every day with real heartiness. What does this show? | Loss of memory | Sadness | Being a bit grumpy | *Strength and good health
test: The host's heartiness made every guest feel welcome. What does heartiness mean? | Wealth | *Warm, cheerful friendliness | Anger | Silence
test: Which meaning of heartiness fits a hearty breakfast? | Being lost | Cheerful friendliness | Quiet thinking | *Large, filling and satisfying
exam: In «the heartiness of the crowd's cheers», what does heartiness mean? | A small, empty plate | Cold, quiet respect | *Warm, cheerful energy | Ill health
